# biotracker — screen wireframes

Layout-only ASCII mocks for the design/token retake. 11 representative screens
covering every distinct layout pattern. Settings CRUD list/one pairs are
represented once each (datapoint list + datapoint one) since the others
(chart, category, notification) share the same shell.

## Shell primitives
- **TabScreen**: SafeArea + ScrollView, `background`, 12px vertical pad. Bottom tab bar.
- **StackScreen**: SafeArea + optional ScrollView, `background`. Native stack header w/ back arrow + title + headerRight.
- **Bottom tabs**: Input | Charts. 2px top divider, active=`accent`, inactive=`text__label`.
- **FAB (MenuButton)**: 56×56 circle, `primary`, bottom-right, white plus.

## Screens
1. 01-input-home         — Input tab dashboard (banner + card sections + FAB)
2. 02-input-entry-list   — entries for one datapoint (calendar swipe header)
3. 03-input-entry-one    — single entry form (value input + timestamp)
4. 04-input-entry-all    — quick-log every datapoint (paged nav)
5. 05-charts             — chart view + chart selector
6. 06-settings-home      — settings menu (grouped list)
7. 07-settings-appearance— theme picker (System/Light/Dark)
8. 08-settings-profile   — profile info
9. 09-settings-list      — generic CRUD list (datapoints, grouped by category)
10. 10-settings-one      — generic CRUD detail/edit form
